index 5328810..fa13012 100644
--- a/CAPTAIN.md
+++ b/CAPTAIN.md
@@ -71,7 +71,27 @@ Two further browser-only acceptance defects, pinned as new scenarios on `watchbi
   source level by a `@contract` page-reference pin:
   - `features/todomvc.feature:The served page links the application stylesheet`
   Crew fix: add the stylesheet `<link>` to `index.html` (CSS chain per build intent:
-  `todomvc-common/base.css`, `todomvc-app-css/index.css`, then `css/app.css`).
+  `todomvc-common/base.css`, `todmvc-app-css/index.css`, then `css/app.css`).
+
+- **Empty-edit commit throws removeChild in a real browser (acceptance: Editing, should
+  remove the item if an empty text string was entered).** Committing an edit that empties the
+  text removes the item but never ends the editing session: `commitEdit` leaves the `editing`
+  class on the removed list item and calls `render()`. In a real browser, removing the focused
+  edit `<input>` during that render fires a synchronous `blur`; `handleEditBlur` re-invokes
+  `commitEdit`, whose `render()` detaches the same `<li>` before the outer `removeChild` runs,
+  so `render` at `js/app.js:134` throws `NotFoundError: ... no longer a child ... moved in a
+  'blur' event handler`. happy-dom does NOT fire `blur` on removal (verified in-harness:
+  `blur fired after removeChild: false`), and a manual blur on the already-detached node is
+  harmless, so the in-harness suite cannot reproduce it. The pin is source-level, not
+  behavioural:
+  - `features/todomvc.feature:The edit-commit path discharges its re-entrancy guard`
+    (tagged `@conformance`, references `scantlings/edit-commit.json`). The QM-owned bespoke
+    checker reads `js/app.js` and reddens while the edit session is not ended on commit.
+  Crew fix: end the editing session before the post-commit re-render, e.g. remove the
+  `editing` class from the list item in `commitEdit` (any branch that re-renders), so the
+  blur handler's `editing`-class guard makes the re-entrant call a no-op. A `render`-level
+  `parentNode` guard on `removeChild` is an acceptable alternative; either turns the check
+  green.
 
